WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.740
Private retrieval-augmented generation, often called private RAG,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.133
can help AI systems answer from approved internal material.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.396
It can also create new responsibilities.

00:00:08.396 --> 00:00:12.544
Source documents must be ingested, chunked, embedded, indexed, retrieved, cited, updated,

00:00:12.544 --> 00:00:13.675
expired, and permissioned.

00:00:13.675 --> 00:00:19.709
Treating RAG as only a vector database misses the governance work that makes the knowledge trustworthy.

00:00:19.709 --> 00:00:22.726
Knowledge control starts with source ownership and provenance.

00:00:22.726 --> 00:00:26.874
Teams should know where a document came from, who owns it,

00:00:26.874 --> 00:00:31.776
when it was ingested, what version it represents, and whether it is current.

00:00:31.776 --> 00:00:36.301
Metadata matters because the AI system may retrieve fragments without the original

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:39.318
context that humans normally use to judge authority,

00:00:39.318 --> 00:00:40.449
audience, and freshness.

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:41.957
Permissions must survive retrieval.

00:00:41.957 --> 00:00:46.482
A user should not receive content through an AI answer that they

00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:49.122
could not access through the source system.

00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:51.385
Tenant boundaries, document-level permissions, collection-level permissions,

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:53.270
and query-time enforcement all matter.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:58.926
It is not enough to protect the storage location if retrieval ignores the access rules.

00:00:58.926 --> 00:01:01.566
RAG quality also depends on lifecycle discipline.

00:01:01.566 --> 00:01:04.206
Old guidance can be retrieved as current.

00:01:04.206 --> 00:01:06.091
Chunks can lose important qualifiers.

00:01:06.091 --> 00:01:08.731
Conflicting sources can appear side by side.

00:01:08.731 --> 00:01:11.370
Sensitive documents can enter the wrong collection.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.764
A sovereign AI program needs reviewable ingestion, retrieval testing,

00:01:14.764 --> 00:01:18.158
source citations where appropriate, expiration rules, and update workflows.

00:01:18.158 --> 00:01:20.421
Retrieved text is context and evidence;

00:01:20.421 --> 00:01:25.700
it should not be treated as unlimited authority over policy, law, or operational judgment.
